  "full_response": "Certainly! Below is a Python function that calculates the Fibonacci sequence using dynamic programming. This implementation uses an iterative approach for space optimization.\n\n```python\ndef fibonacci(n):\n    # Handle base cases\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the first two Fibonacci numbers\n    fib_0 = 0\n    fib_1 = 1\n\n    # Calculate Fibonacci numbers iteratively\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_0 + fib_1\n        fib_0 = fib_1\n        fib_1 = next_fib\n\n    return fib_1\n\n# Example usage:\nn = 10\nprint(f\"The {n}th Fibonacci number is: {fibonacci(n)}\")\n```\n\nYou can call the `fibonacci` function with any non-negative integer `n` to find the `n`! Fibonacci number. This function uses only O(1) extra space and O(n) time, making it efficient for calculating large Fibonacci numbers.",
